{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793473481,"nonce":"0OciElXT8h0qyiARF4e44jmlM1A=","title":"LLVM build fails on Ubuntu's llvm-21-dev: Polly and zstd","message":"Reported by the dynASB embedding session (their git-bug 5b7d11d) on Ubuntu 26.04. `--features llvm-backend` fails to link llvm-sys with \"could not find native static library Polly\" (the distro ships no libPolly.a), then \"unable to find library -lzstd\" (no libzstd.so dev symlink). Empty libPolly.a/libPollyISL.a stubs and a libzstd.so symlink in a -L directory get past both; LLVM_SYS_211_PREFER_DYNAMIC=1 does not change the first error. The build should not require Polly, and should find zstd as the distro installs it or take a dynamic LLVM.","files":null}]}